# EcoTrace India — environment configuration index
#
# This is a monorepo; there is no single shared .env. Each runnable service
# has its own environment template — copy the one(s) you need, never commit
# the resulting .env file (see .gitignore).
#
#   backend/.env.example                — Node/Express/Prisma API (auth, submissions, rewards)
#   intelligence/device_ai/.env.example — Python/FastAPI AI service (detection, passports, Fabric Gateway)
#   frontend/.env.example               — React/Vite admin & stakeholder dashboard
#
# Mobile apps (mobile/collector_app, mobile/consumer_app) are configured at
# build time via --dart-define, not a .env file — see
# mobile/*/lib/core/config/app_config.dart.
#
# docker-compose.yml reads POSTGRES_* variables for the local Postgres
# container; see that file's own comments for the variables it accepts.
#
# ECOTRACE_DATASET_ROOT — external dataset location (2026-09 migration moved
# the ~29GB acquired training/staging/evaluation/candidate data out of the
# repo to keep it out of Git). Set it as a real OS environment variable (a
# repo-root .env only feeds docker-compose's own variable substitution — it
# is NOT read by Python code, which reads the OS environment directly via
# acquisition.config.dataset_acquisition_root()). Example:
#   ECOTRACE_DATASET_ROOT=E:\Ecotrace Dataset
# When unset, both docker-compose.yml and the Python acquisition/training
# code fall back to the original in-repo dataset_acquisition/ location, so
# a machine that hasn't migrated keeps working unchanged.
